      "description": "A candlelight vigil-protest of thousands of people was held on the large main street Sejong-daero in Jung-gu, Seoul near Seoul City Hall for the victims of the Seoul Halloween crowd crush at the end of the mourning period on Saturday, November 5, 2022. It was held by the progressive group Candlelight Action, who have held prior regular protests against the government of President Yoon Suk-yeol, and was based at City Hall Subway Station, Exit 7, starting at 5:00 p.m. This is a photo of police guarding the end of the protest area, which extended on two lanes of the major street from the subway exit to the traffic light by Sungnyemun Gate (on the left side across the street).",
